flowchart LR
    D[IoT devices and edge services<br/>telemetry, commands, state] -->|ZMV/1 over TCP<br/>AUTH + ACL| E[Local ZigMV edge broker]

    E --> L[live<br/>volatile, low latency]
    E --> W[work<br/>one worker per group]
    E --> U[durable<br/>ACK + bounded retry<br/>connected session]
    E --> S[state<br/>retained last value + expiry]

    U --> Q[Bounded local stream / pending delivery state]
    S --> R[Retained state index]

    E -->|subject export filter| X[Authenticated edge link<br/>TLS/mTLS pending release gate]
    X -->|reconnect + cursor transfer<br/>bounded queue| C[Regional or cloud ZigMV broker]

    C --> A[Cloud services and consumers]
    C --> N[NATS compatibility adapter<br/>Core / request-reply boundary]
    C --> M[MQTT 5.0 compatibility adapter<br/>QoS/session boundary]

    Q -.->|offline configured profiles<br/>future transfer| X
    X -.->|link lag, retries, drops, reconnect metrics| O[Operations and observability]
    E -.-> O
    C -.-> O

    classDef edge fill:#0b5,stroke:#083,color:#fff;
    classDef cloud fill:#246,stroke:#123,color:#fff;
    classDef profile fill:#f4f1de,stroke:#765,color:#111;
    classDef ops fill:#ddd,stroke:#666,color:#111;
    class E,X edge;
    class C,A,N,M cloud;
    class L,W,U,S,Q,R profile;
    class O ops;
    linkStyle 7,8 stroke-dasharray: 5 5;

%% Guarantees:
%% live ~= Core NATS / MQTT QoS 0
%% durable currently ~= connected-session ACK/retry, not MQTT QoS 2
%% exact and full MQTT QoS 2 remain future release gates
